# Crypto Watcher — Smart Contracts

> Phase tags (`MVP`, `Phase 1`, `Phase 2`, `Phase 3`, `Final`) cite
> [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.mdc). Keep this file in sync with the roadmap and with the
> actual `contracts/` implementation (see the docs-sync rule in `.cursor/rules/`).

## Tech Stack

- Solidity + Foundry (`forge`, `cast`, `anvil`) — see [README](../README.md).
- OpenZeppelin contracts for `ERC20Votes`, `Governor`, `TimelockController`,
  `AccessControl`.
- Consumed on the frontend via Viem + Wagmi.

## Modular Folder Structure

The contracts package is organized by domain module. Each module owns its
contracts, interfaces, tests and deploy scripts.

```
contracts/
├── foundry.toml
├── remappings.txt
├── lib/                          # forge dependencies (OpenZeppelin, forge-std)
├── src/
│   ├── governance/               # Governance module
│   │   ├── GovernanceToken.sol   # ERC20Votes governance token  [MVP]
│   │   ├── CryptoWatcherGovernor.sol  # Governor (proposals/voting)  [MVP→Final]
│   │   ├── Timelock.sol          # TimelockController             [MVP]
│   │   └── interfaces/
│   ├── voting/                   # Per-project voting module
│   │   ├── ProjectVoting.sol     # Per-project vote/tally/close   [MVP]
│   │   ├── ProjectVotingFactory.sol  # Deploys per-project contracts  [MVP]
│   │   └── interfaces/
│   ├── reputation/               # Reputation & eligibility module
│   │   ├── ReputationRegistry.sol # Eligibility + weight source   [MVP→Phase 1]
│   │   └── interfaces/
│   ├── rewards/                  # Voter rewards module
│   │   ├── RewardDistributor.sol # Reward + slashing              [Phase 1]
│   │   └── interfaces/
│   ├── access/                   # Shared access control / roles
│   │   └── Roles.sol
│   └── libraries/                # Shared libraries (math, scoring)
├── script/                       # forge deploy scripts (per module)
├── test/                         # mirrors src/ module layout
│   ├── governance/
│   ├── voting/
│   └── reputation/
└── deployments/                  # per-chain deployed addresses (json)
```

## Modules by Phase

### Governance module — launch requirement
- `GovernanceToken` (`ERC20Votes`): token + delegation support. `[MVP]`
- Seed distribution to trustworthy users. `[MVP]`
- `Timelock` (`TimelockController`) owned by team multisig at launch. `[MVP]`
- `CryptoWatcherGovernor`: minimal proposals for protocol params (voting duration,
  reputation threshold). `[MVP]`
- Community token-weighted proposals, quorum + voting delay. `[Phase 1]`
- Vote delegation UX support. `[Phase 2]`
- Full DAO: treasury + upgrade control governed on-chain. `[Final]`

### Voting module
- `ProjectVoting`: cast vote, close, tally; lifecycle states matching the
  README flow (`Ready → Voting → Closed → Analyzed`). `[MVP]`
- `ProjectVotingFactory`: deploys one voting contract per project. `[MVP]`
- Reputation-gated voting (only eligible wallets). `[MVP]`
- Reputation-weighted vote power (basic, single-factor). `[MVP]`
- Tiered vote weight by reputation. `[Phase 1]`
- Multi-chain deployment of voting contracts. `[Phase 2]`

### Reputation module
- `ReputationRegistry`: eligibility allow-list + basic weight. `[MVP]`
- Multi-factor reputation (accuracy, tenure, staking, decay). `[Phase 1]`
- On-chain reputation portability. `[Phase 2]`
- Decentralized reputation / verifiable credentials. `[Final]`

### Rewards module
- `RewardDistributor`: distribute governance tokens for accurate votes. `[Phase 1]`
- Slashing / penalties for malicious voting. `[Phase 1]`
- Sustainable reward tokenomics + treasury funding. `[Final]`

## Scoring

- Project score computed from on-chain tallies; weighting by reputation. `[MVP]`
- Score factors enriched with external risk signals (data providers). `[Phase 3]`
- Advanced automated + community hybrid risk model. `[Phase 3]`

## Security & Testing

- Foundry unit + fuzz tests per module, CI security scanning. `[MVP]`
- External audits scaling with phase. `[Phase 2 → Final]`
- Formal verification of core contracts. `[Final]`

## Conventions

- One module = one folder under `src/`, with matching `test/` and `script/` folders.
- Interfaces live in each module's `interfaces/` folder.
- Deployed addresses tracked per chain in `deployments/`.
- Use `AccessControl` roles (from `access/Roles.sol`) instead of bare `onlyOwner`.
